PathwayData.put("data/grammar_vocabulary/units/L02U5.json",{"strand":"grammar_vocabulary","level":2,"cefr":"A1b","unit":5,"theme":"Clothes and Shopping","essential_question":"How do we make good choices when we shop?","lessons":[{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS1","title":"I Love Them! Object Pronouns","objectives":["Students will be able to use object pronouns after verbs and prepositions.","Students will be able to replace nouns with object pronouns to avoid repetition.","I can say \"I like them\" and \"Give it to me\".","I can use him, her and them instead of names."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام ضمائر المفعول بعد الأفعال وحروف الجر.","سيتمكن الطلاب من استبدال الأسماء بضمائر المفعول لتجنب التكرار.","أستطيع أن أقول I like them وGive it to me.","أستطيع أن أستخدم him وher وthem بدلًا من الأسماء."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"shirt","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ʃɝt/","definition":"a piece of clothing for the top of your body, with buttons","arabic":"قميص","example":"His school shirt is white.","image_id":"GV-L02-U5-LS1-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U5-LS1-W01"},{"word":"thobe","pos":"noun","ipa":"/θoʊb/","definition":"a long robe that men and boys wear in Saudi Arabia","arabic":"ثوب","example":"Dad wears a white thobe on Friday.","image_id":"GV-L02-U5-LS1-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U5-LS1-W02"},{"word":"dress","pos":"noun","ipa":"/drɛs/","definition":"a piece of clothing for girls and women, from the shoulders down","arabic":"فستان","example":"Lina's dress is long and green.","image_id":"GV-L02-U5-LS1-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U5-LS1-W03"},{"word":"shoes","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ʃuz/","definition":"things you wear on your feet when you go out","arabic":"حذاء","example":"Put your shoes by the door.","image_id":"GV-L02-U5-LS1-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U5-LS1-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"Object pronouns come after a verb or a preposition: I like them. Give it to me.\nWe use them so we don't repeat a noun: I like the sneakers. I want them (= the sneakers).\nSubject pronouns come before the verb (I, he, she, we, they). Object pronouns come after (me, him, her, us, them).\nI → me • you → you • he → him • she → her\nit → it • we → us • they → them\nAfter a verb: Call him. • After a preposition: Come with us.","examples":["These socks are soft. I like them.","Can you help me, please?","Sara is at the shop. Call her.","Where is my cap? I can't find it.","Mr. Khalid is kind. We love him.","Wait for us! We're coming.","Give the bags to them.","This scarf is for you."],"common_errors":["✗ I like this shirt. I want to buy it shirt. → ✓ I like this shirt. I want to buy it. (Use it instead of repeating the noun.)","✗ Give the bag to I. → ✓ Give the bag to me. (After to → object pronoun.)","✗ I like Ali. I play with he. → ✓ I like Ali. I play with him. (After with → him.)","✗ The shoes are nice. I like it. → ✓ The shoes are nice. I like them. (shoes is plural → them.)"],"arabic":"ضمائر المفعول تأتي بعد الفعل أو حرف الجر: I like them (أحبها).\nI → me، he → him، she → her، we → us، they → them، it → it.\nلا نقول Give it to I، بل Give it to me.\nإذا كان الاسم جمعًا (shoes) نستخدم them وليس it."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “I Love Them! Object Pronouns”. Let’s learn object pronouns (me, you, him, her, it, us, them) together.","on_screen":"GV-L02-U5-LS1 | I Love Them! Object Pronouns","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Listen to the start of “At the Shoe Shop”: Omar: Dad, look at these sneakers! I really like them. Look at the green words.","on_screen":"Omar: Dad, look at these sneakers! I really like them.","visual":"Image GV-L02-U5-LS1-IMG01 animates gently; target words glow Leaf Green as they are spoken."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Object pronouns come after a verb or a preposition: I like them. Give it to me. We use them so we don't repeat a noun: I like the sneakers. I want them (= the sneakers).","on_screen":"I → me • you → you • he → him • she → her • it → it • we → us • they → them • After a verb: Call him. • After a preposition: Come with us.","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. These socks are soft. I like them. Can you help me, please? Sara is at the shop. Call her.","on_screen":"These socks are soft. I like them. / Can you help me, please? / Sara is at the shop. Call her.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “I like this shirt. I want to buy it shirt.” That’s not right. We say: “I like this shirt. I want to buy it.” Use it instead of repeating the noun.","on_screen":"✗ I like this shirt. I want to buy it shirt.   ✓ I like this shirt. I want to buy it.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"I like the sneakers. I want them.\" What does \"them\" mean? … Think! … The sneakers. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"I like them\" and \"Give it to me\".","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"I like them\" and \"Give it to me\".","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: object pronouns (me, you, him, her, it, us, them).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","ضمائر المفعول تأتي بعد الفعل أو حرف الجر: I like them (أحبها).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: I like this shirt. I want to buy it shirt. — الصحيح: I like this shirt. I want to buy it.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول I like them وGive it to me."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"At the Shoe Shop","body":"Omar: Dad, look at these sneakers! I really like them.\nDad: They're nice. Try them on.\nOmar: Oh, they're too small for me. Do you have them in size 36?\nAssistant: Yes. Here you are.\nOmar: They're perfect! How much are they?\nAssistant: They're 150 riyals.\nDad: OK, we'll take them. And Yusuf wants a blue cap. Can you show us one?\nAssistant: Sure. Here's a blue cap. Do you like it?\nDad: Yes. Yusuf will love it!","word_count":78,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U5-LS1-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS1-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","items":[{"q":"These shoes are great. I want ___.","options":["it","them","they","their"],"answer":"them","explanation":"they / plural things → them.","explanation_ar":"الجمع ← them."},{"q":"Can you help ___, please? I'm lost.","options":["my","mine","me","I"],"answer":"me","explanation":"I → me after a verb or preposition.","explanation_ar":"I تصبح me بعد الفعل أو حرف الجر."},{"q":"Rakan is my cousin. I play with ___ every day.","options":["them","him","he","his"],"answer":"him","explanation":"he → him.","explanation_ar":"he تصبح him."},{"q":"Noura has a new dress. Look at ___!","options":["hers","she","him","her"],"answer":"her","explanation":"she → her.","explanation_ar":"she تصبح her."},{"q":"This cap is nice. How much is ___?","options":["it","they","its","them"],"answer":"it","explanation":"one thing → it.","explanation_ar":"الشيء الواحد ← it."},{"q":"We're at the mall. Come with ___!","options":["we","them","us","our"],"answer":"us","explanation":"we → us.","explanation_ar":"we تصبح us."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS1-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Replace the underlined words with a pronoun.","items":[{"q":"I see my cousins.  (pronoun)","options":[],"answer":"I see them.","explanation":"they / plural things → them.","explanation_ar":"الجمع ← them."},{"q":"Call your dad, please.  (pronoun)","options":[],"answer":"Call him, please.","explanation":"he → him.","explanation_ar":"he تصبح him."},{"q":"I bought the scarf for my mom.  (pronouns)","options":[],"answer":"I bought it for her.","explanation":"she → her.","explanation_ar":"she تصبح her."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS1-B2","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Write me, him, her, it, us or them. Word bank: us, him, them","items":[{"q":"Sara and I are in the shop. Please wait for ______.","options":[],"answer":"us","explanation":"we → us.","explanation_ar":"we تصبح us."},{"q":"My grandpa loves dates. I bring ______ dates every week.","options":[],"answer":"him","explanation":"he → him.","explanation_ar":"he تصبح him."},{"q":"Where are my socks? I can't find ______.","options":[],"answer":"them","explanation":"they / plural things → them.","explanation_ar":"الجمع ← them."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS1-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Answer the questions with object pronouns.","items":[{"q":"Do you like sneakers?","options":[],"answer":"Yes, I like them.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses object pronouns (me, you, him, her, it, us, them) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Do you help your mom?","options":[],"answer":"Yes, I help her every day.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses object pronouns (me, you, him, her, it, us, them) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Do you visit your grandparents?","options":[],"answer":"Yes, I visit them on Friday.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses object pronouns (me, you, him, her, it, us, them) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Who teaches you English?","options":[],"answer":"Mr. Khalid teaches us English.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses object pronouns (me, you, him, her, it, us, them) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Do you play football with your brother?","options":[],"answer":"Yes, I play with him after school.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses object pronouns (me, you, him, her, it, us, them) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS1-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Gift time.","items":[{"q":"Choose a gift for 3 people. Write who it is for with him/her/them.","options":[],"answer":"I'm buying a cap for Ziyad. It's for him. I'm buying scarves for my sisters. They're for them.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses object pronouns (me, you, him, her, it, us, them) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences asking for help in a shop with me/us.","options":[],"answer":"Can you help me? Can you show us the red shoes?","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses object pronouns (me, you, him, her, it, us, them) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Read your gifts to a partner. Write one gift he chooses.","options":[],"answer":"He chooses a watch for his dad. It's for him.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses object pronouns (me, you, him, her, it, us, them) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Four Corners Grammar","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["The teacher says a sentence frame with a cue word and four possible answers (A–D).","Students walk to the corner with the correct answer.","One student in each corner explains the choice in one sentence.","Correct corner scores a point; continue with the next cue."],"data":[{"label":"Can you help ___? (me)"},{"label":"I like ___. (the shoes → them)"},{"label":"Give it to ___. (Sara → her)"},{"label":"Call ___. (Dad → him)"},{"label":"Wait for ___. (my friend and me → us)"},{"label":"I want ___. (the cap → it)"},{"label":"Ask ___. (the shop assistant → her)"},{"label":"Show ___. (the boys → them)"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"I like these socks. Can I try ___ on?","options":["its","they","them","it"],"answer":"them","explanation":"they / plural things → them.","explanation_ar":"الجمع ← them."},{"q":"Please give the receipt to ___.","options":["I","me","my","mine"],"answer":"me","explanation":"I → me after a verb or preposition.","explanation_ar":"I تصبح me بعد الفعل أو حرف الجر."},{"q":"My aunt is here. Say hello to ___.","options":["hers","him","her","she"],"answer":"her","explanation":"she → her.","explanation_ar":"she تصبح her."},{"q":"Where's my scarf? I need ___.","options":["one it","them","it","its"],"answer":"it","explanation":"one thing → it.","explanation_ar":"الشيء الواحد ← it."},{"q":"","options":["Majed is my friend. I go to school with he.","Majed is my friend. I go to school with them.","Majed is my friend. I go to school with his.","Majed is my friend. I go to school with him."],"answer":"Majed is my friend. I go to school with him.","explanation":"he → him.","explanation_ar":"he تصبح him."},{"q":"My little sisters are tired. Let's carry ___.","options":["them","they","their","it"],"answer":"them","explanation":"they / plural things → them.","explanation_ar":"الجمع ← them."},{"q":"","options":["Can you show us the blue caps?","Can you show our the blue caps?","Can you show we the blue caps?","Can you show us it the blue caps?"],"answer":"Can you show us the blue caps?","explanation":"we → us.","explanation_ar":"we تصبح us."},{"q":"Mom bought a new phone. She loves ___.","options":["its","them","her","it"],"answer":"it","explanation":"one thing → it.","explanation_ar":"الشيء الواحد ← it."},{"q":"","options":["Dad is waiting for you and I.","Dad is waiting for you and me.","Dad is waiting for your and me.","Dad is waiting for you and my."],"answer":"Dad is waiting for you and me.","explanation":"I → me after a verb or preposition.","explanation_ar":"I تصبح me بعد الفعل أو حرف الجر."},{"q":"The shop assistant is helpful. Ask ___ about sizes.","options":["her","hers","they","she"],"answer":"her","explanation":"she → her.","explanation_ar":"she تصبح her."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS1-IMG01","prompt":"Omar and his dad in a shoe shop; Omar holding up a pair of blue sneakers while a smiling shop assistant brings a box. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Omar and his dad in a shoe shop; Omar holding up a pair of blue sneakers while a smiling shop assistant brings a box"},{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS1-IMG02","prompt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about object pronouns (me, you, him, her, it, us, them), with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right; leave large empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about object pronouns (me, you, him, her, it, us, them), with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right"},{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS1-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows shirt (a piece of clothing for the top of your body, with buttons); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing shirt: a piece of clothing for the top of your body, with buttons"},{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS1-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows thobe (a long robe that men and boys wear in Saudi Arabia); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing thobe: a long robe that men and boys wear in Saudi Arabia"},{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS1-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows dress (a piece of clothing for girls and women, from the shoulders down); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing dress: a piece of clothing for girls and women, from the shoulders down"},{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS1-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows shoes (things you wear on your feet when you go out); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing shoes: things you wear on your feet when you go out"},{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS1-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Four Corners Grammar”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Four Corners Grammar"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U5-LS1-W01","script":"shirt. shirt. His school shirt is white.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U5-LS1-W02","script":"thobe. thobe. Dad wears a white thobe on Friday.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U5-LS1-W03","script":"dress. dress. Lina's dress is long and green.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U5-LS1-W04","script":"shoes. shoes. Put your shoes by the door.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U5-LS1-T1","script":"Omar: Dad, look at these sneakers! I really like them. Dad: They're nice. Try them on. Omar: Oh, they're too small for me. Do you have them in size 36? Assistant: Yes. Here you are. Omar: They're perfect! How much are they? Assistant: They're 150 riyals. Dad: OK, we'll take them. And Yusuf wants a blue cap. Can you show us one? Assistant: Sure. Here's a blue cap. Do you like it? Dad: Yes. Yusuf will love it!","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U5-LS1-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “I Love Them! Object Pronouns”. Let’s learn object pronouns (me, you, him, her, it, us, them) together. Listen to the start of “At the Shoe Shop”: Omar: Dad, look at these sneakers! I really like them. Look at the green words. Object pronouns come after a verb or a preposition: I like them. Give it to me. We use them so we don't repeat a noun: I like the sneakers. I want them (= the sneakers). Here are some examples. These socks are soft. I like them. Can you help me, please? Sara is at the shop. Call her. Be careful! Some learners say: “I like this shirt. I want to buy it shirt.” That’s not right. We say: “I like this shirt. I want to buy it.” Use it instead of repeating the noun. Quick check: \"I like the sneakers. I want them.\" What does \"them\" mean? … Think! … The sneakers. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"I like them\" and \"Give it to me\".","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS2","title":"How Much Is It? Prices with this, these and How many","objectives":["Students will be able to ask and answer about prices with How much is this…? / How much are these…?","Students will be able to ask How many…? about numbers of things.","I can ask \"How much are these socks?\"","I can ask \"How many caps do you have?\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من السؤال عن الأسعار والإجابة باستخدام How much is/are…?","سيتمكن الطلاب من السؤال عن العدد باستخدام How many…?","أستطيع أن أسأل How much are these socks?","أستطيع أن أسأل How many caps do you have?"],"vocabulary":[{"word":"sneakers","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈsnikɚz/","definition":"soft sports shoes (American English)","arabic":"حذاء رياضي","example":"My sneakers are good for running.","image_id":"GV-L02-U5-LS2-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U5-LS2-W01"},{"word":"socks","pos":"noun","ipa":"/sɑks/","definition":"soft things you wear on your feet inside shoes","arabic":"جوارب","example":"These socks keep my feet warm.","image_id":"GV-L02-U5-LS2-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U5-LS2-W02"},{"word":"cap","pos":"noun","ipa":"/kæp/","definition":"a soft hat with a hard part at the front","arabic":"قبعة (كاب)","example":"Adam wears his cap backward.","image_id":"GV-L02-U5-LS2-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U5-LS2-W03"},{"word":"scarf","pos":"noun","ipa":"/skɑrf/","definition":"a long piece of cloth you wear around your neck","arabic":"وشاح","example":"Grandma knits a red scarf.","image_id":"GV-L02-U5-LS2-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U5-LS2-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"To ask about the price of one thing, say How much is this/that + noun? – It's 20 riyals.\nFor two or more things, say How much are these/those + plural noun? – They're 30 riyals.\nTo ask about a number of things, say How many + plural noun? How many shirts do you have? – I have five.","examples":["How much is this dress? – It's 90 riyals.","How much are these shoes? – They're 120 riyals.","How much is that scarf? – It's only 10 riyals.","How many socks are in the pack? – There are five pairs.","How many caps do you need? – I need three.","These gloves are cheap.","That jacket is too expensive.","How much are those bags over there?"],"common_errors":["✗ How much this shirt? → ✓ How much is this shirt? (Don't forget is.)","✗ How much is these socks? → ✓ How much are these socks? (Plural → are these.)","✗ How many is the cap? → ✓ How much is the cap? (Price → How much.)","✗ How many shirt do you have? → ✓ How many shirts do you have? (After How many, use a plural noun.)"],"arabic":"للسؤال عن سعر شيء واحد: How much is this…? والإجابة: It's 20 riyals.\nللسؤال عن سعر أكثر من شيء: How much are these…? والإجابة: They're…\nHow many للسؤال عن العدد، ويأتي بعدها اسم جمع: How many shirts?"},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “How Much Is It? Prices with this, these and How many”. Let’s learn How much is/are…? (prices) and How many…? (numbers) with this/these together.","on_screen":"GV-L02-U5-LS2 | How Much Is It? Prices with this, these and How many","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Remember these patterns: This shirt is 40 riyals. • These socks are 15 riyals. That watch isn't cheap. • These shoes aren't expensive. How much is this cap? – It's 25 riyals. • How much are these sneakers? – They're 150 riyals. • How many scarves do you want? – Two, please.","on_screen":"This shirt is 40 riyals. • These socks are 15 riyals. | That watch isn't cheap. • These shoes aren't expensive. | How much is this cap? – It's 25 riyals. • How much are these sneakers? – They're 150 riyals. • How many scarves do you want? – Two, please.","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"To ask about the price of one thing, say How much is this/that + noun? – It's 20 riyals. For two or more things, say How much are these/those + plural noun? – They're 30 riyals.","on_screen":"How much is/are…? (prices) and How many…? (numbers) with this/these","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. How much is this dress? – It's 90 riyals. How much are these shoes? – They're 120 riyals. How much is that scarf? – It's only 10 riyals.","on_screen":"How much is this dress? – It's 90 riyals. / How much are these shoes? – They're 120 riyals. / How much is that scarf? – It's only 10 riyals.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “How much this shirt?.” That’s not right. We say: “How much is this shirt?.” Don't forget is.","on_screen":"✗ How much this shirt?   ✓ How much is this shirt?","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: Do we ask \"How much\" or \"How many\" about a price? … Think! … *How much*. Great job! Now you can say: I can ask \"How much are these socks?\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can ask \"How much are these socks?\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: How much is/are…? (prices) and How many…? (numbers) with this/these.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","للسؤال عن سعر شيء واحد: How much is this…? والإجابة: It's 20 riyals.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: How much this shirt? — الصحيح: How much is this shirt?","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أسأل How much are these socks?"]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS2-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"How much ___ this scarf?","options":["does","do","is","are"],"answer":"is","explanation":"One thing → How much is this/that…? – It's…","explanation_ar":"للمفرد: How much is this."},{"q":"How much are ___ shoes?","options":["these","it","this","that"],"answer":"these","explanation":"Plural → How much are these/those…? – They're…","explanation_ar":"للجمع: How much are these."},{"q":"How much is this cap? – ___ 30 riyals.","options":["Is","It's","There's","They're"],"answer":"It's","explanation":"One thing → How much is this/that…? – It's…","explanation_ar":"للمفرد: How much is this."},{"q":"How much are those socks? – ___ 12 riyals.","options":["They're","Is","There are","It's"],"answer":"They're","explanation":"Plural → How much are these/those…? – They're…","explanation_ar":"للجمع: How much are these."},{"q":"___ shirts do you want? – Three, please.","options":["What many","How much","How","How many"],"answer":"How many","explanation":"Number → How many + plural noun?","explanation_ar":"للعدد: How many + جمع."},{"q":"___ is that dress? – It's 75 riyals.","options":["What much","How many","How","How much"],"answer":"How much","explanation":"Price → How much (not How many).","explanation_ar":"السعر ← How much."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS2-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Make questions about prices.","items":[{"q":"this jacket  (How much)","options":[],"answer":"How much is this jacket?","explanation":"One thing → How much is this/that…? – It's…","explanation_ar":"للمفرد: How much is this."},{"q":"these sandals  (How much)","options":[],"answer":"How much are these sandals?","explanation":"Plural → How much are these/those…? – They're…","explanation_ar":"للجمع: How much are these."},{"q":"that bag  (How much)","options":[],"answer":"How much is that bag?","explanation":"One thing → How much is this/that…? – It's…","explanation_ar":"للمفرد: How much is this."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS2-B2","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Write How much or How many. Word bank: How much, How many","items":[{"q":"______ pencils are in the box?","options":[],"answer":"How many","explanation":"Number → How many + plural noun?","explanation_ar":"للعدد: How many + جمع."},{"q":"______ is the red thobe?","options":[],"answer":"How much","explanation":"Price → How much (not How many).","explanation_ar":"السعر ← How much."},{"q":"______ sisters do you have?","options":[],"answer":"How many","explanation":"Number → How many + plural noun?","explanation_ar":"للعدد: How many + جمع."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS2-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Answer about your things.","items":[{"q":"How many pairs of shoes do you have?","options":[],"answer":"I have four pairs of shoes.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses How much is/are…? (prices) and How many…? (numbers) with this/these correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"How much is a bottle of water in your school canteen?","options":[],"answer":"It's two riyals.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses How much is/are…? (prices) and How many…? (numbers) with this/these correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"How many caps do you have?","options":[],"answer":"I have two caps.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses How much is/are…? (prices) and How many…? (numbers) with this/these correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"How much are your favorite sneakers?","options":[],"answer":"They're 200 riyals.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses How much is/are…? (prices) and How many…? (numbers) with this/these correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"How many people are in your class?","options":[],"answer":"There are twenty-four students in my class.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses How much is/are…? (prices) and How many…? (numbers) with this/these correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS2-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Shop role-play.","items":[{"q":"Make 4 price tags for clothes. Write them.","options":[],"answer":"cap – 25 riyals; socks – 10 riyals; scarf – 35 riyals; sneakers – 180 riyals","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses How much is/are…? (prices) and How many…? (numbers) with this/these correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a 6-line dialogue between a customer and a seller with How much and How many.","options":[],"answer":"A: How much is this cap? B: It's 25 riyals. A: How much are these socks? B: They're 10 riyals. A: How many pairs do you have? B: We have six.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses How much is/are…? (prices) and How many…? (numbers) with this/these correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Act it out. Write the total price your partner pays.","options":[],"answer":"He pays 45 riyals.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses How much is/are…? (prices) and How many…? (numbers) with this/these correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Grammar Snakes & Ladders","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["Roll and move. If you land on a cue square, make a sentence with the cue and How much is/are…? (prices) and How many…? (numbers) with this/these.","Correct at the bottom of a ladder: climb. Incorrect at the head of a snake: slide down.","Teammates are the judges and must explain any correction.","First player to reach square 30 wins."],"data":[{"cue":"How much / this shirt / ?"},{"cue":"How much / these socks / ?"},{"cue":"How many / caps / ?"},{"cue":"this dress / 80 riyals / +"},{"cue":"these shoes / 120 riyals / +"},{"cue":"How many / sizes / ?"},{"cue":"that scarf / cheap / +"},{"cue":"those sneakers / expensive / –"},{"cue":"How much / that thobe / ?"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"How much ___ these sneakers?","options":["do","does","are","is"],"answer":"are","explanation":"Plural → How much are these/those…? – They're…","explanation_ar":"للجمع: How much are these."},{"q":"How much is ___ watch?","options":["they","this","these","those"],"answer":"this","explanation":"One thing → How much is this/that…? – It's…","explanation_ar":"للمفرد: How much is this."},{"q":"How many ___ are in your bag?","options":["bookes","books","a book","book"],"answer":"books","explanation":"Number → How many + plural noun?","explanation_ar":"للعدد: How many + جمع."},{"q":"","options":["How much are that scarf?","How many is that scarf?","How much that scarf?","How much is that scarf?"],"answer":"How much is that scarf?","explanation":"One thing → How much is this/that…? – It's…","explanation_ar":"للمفرد: How much is this."},{"q":"How much are these gloves? – ___","options":["There are 18 riyals.","They 18 riyals.","It's 18 riyals.","They're 18 riyals."],"answer":"They're 18 riyals.","explanation":"Plural → How much are these/those…? – They're…","explanation_ar":"للجمع: How much are these."},{"q":"___ do the shoes cost?","options":["How much","How","What many","How many"],"answer":"How much","explanation":"Price → How much (not How many).","explanation_ar":"السعر ← How much."},{"q":"","options":["How much cousins do you have?","How many cousins do you have?","How many cousins you have?","How many cousin do you have?"],"answer":"How many cousins do you have?","explanation":"Number → How many + plural noun?","explanation_ar":"للعدد: How many + جمع."},{"q":"","options":["How much are that caps?","How much is those caps?","How much are those caps?","How many are those caps?"],"answer":"How much are those caps?","explanation":"Plural → How much are these/those…? – They're…","explanation_ar":"للجمع: How much are these."},{"q":"How much is this dress? – ___","options":["It's 60 riyals.","Is 60 riyals.","They're 60 riyals.","It 60 riyals."],"answer":"It's 60 riyals.","explanation":"One thing → How much is this/that…? – It's…","explanation_ar":"للمفرد: How much is this."},{"q":"___ students are in your class?","options":["What much","How","How much","How many"],"answer":"How many","explanation":"Number → How many + plural noun?","explanation_ar":"للعدد: How many + جمع."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS2-IMG01","prompt":"A colorful market stall with price tags on scarves, caps and socks; Sara pointing at a scarf and asking the seller its price. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A colorful market stall with price tags on scarves, caps and socks; Sara pointing at a scarf and asking the seller its price"},{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS2-IMG02","prompt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of How much is/are…? (prices) and How many…? (numbers) with this/these: a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “Clothes and Shopping”; empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of How much is/are…? (prices) and How many…? (numbers) with this/these: a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “Clothes and Shopping”"},{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS2-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows sneakers (soft sports shoes (American English)); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing sneakers: soft sports shoes (American English)"},{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS2-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows socks (soft things you wear on your feet inside shoes); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing socks: soft things you wear on your feet inside shoes"},{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS2-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows cap (a soft hat with a hard part at the front); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing cap: a soft hat with a hard part at the front"},{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS2-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows scarf (a long piece of cloth you wear around your neck); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing scarf: a long piece of cloth you wear around your neck"},{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS2-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Grammar Snakes & Ladders”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Grammar Snakes & Ladders"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U5-LS2-W01","script":"sneakers. sneakers. My sneakers are good for running.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U5-LS2-W02","script":"socks. socks. These socks keep my feet warm.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U5-LS2-W03","script":"cap. cap. Adam wears his cap backward.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U5-LS2-W04","script":"scarf. scarf. Grandma knits a red scarf.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U5-LS2-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “How Much Is It? Prices with this, these and How many”. Let’s learn How much is/are…? (prices) and How many…? (numbers) with this/these together. Remember these patterns: This shirt is 40 riyals. • These socks are 15 riyals. That watch isn't cheap. • These shoes aren't expensive. How much is this cap? – It's 25 riyals. • How much are these sneakers? – They're 150 riyals. • How many scarves do you want? – Two, please. To ask about the price of one thing, say How much is this/that + noun? – It's 20 riyals. For two or more things, say How much are these/those + plural noun? – They're 30 riyals. Here are some examples. How much is this dress? – It's 90 riyals. How much are these shoes? – They're 120 riyals. How much is that scarf? – It's only 10 riyals. Be careful! Some learners say: “How much this shirt?.” That’s not right. We say: “How much is this shirt?.” Don't forget is. Quick check: Do we ask \"How much\" or \"How many\" about a price? … Think! … *How much*. Great job! Now you can say: I can ask \"How much are these socks?\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS3","title":"What to Wear: Clothes and Shopping Words","objectives":["Students will be able to name clothes and use a pair of with plural clothes.","Students will be able to use shopping words and phrasal verbs (try on, put on, take off).","I can name clothes and say \"a pair of socks\".","I can say \"Try it on\" and \"Take off your shoes\"."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من تسمية الملابس واستخدام a pair of مع الملابس الجمع.","سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام كلمات التسوّق والأفعال المركبة try on وput on وtake off.","أستطيع أن أسمّي الملابس وأقول a pair of socks.","أستطيع أن أقول Try it on وTake off your shoes."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"price","pos":"noun","ipa":"/praɪs/","definition":"how much money something costs","arabic":"سعر","example":"The price is on the label.","image_id":"GV-L02-U5-LS3-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U5-LS3-W01"},{"word":"cheap","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/tʃip/","definition":"not costing a lot of money","arabic":"رخيص","example":"This T-shirt is cheap.","image_id":"GV-L02-U5-LS3-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U5-LS3-W02"},{"word":"expensive","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ɪkˈspɛnsɪv/","definition":"costing a lot of money","arabic":"غالٍ","example":"Gold watches are very expensive.","image_id":"GV-L02-U5-LS3-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U5-LS3-W03"},{"word":"size","pos":"noun","ipa":"/saɪz/","definition":"how big or small something is","arabic":"مقاس / حجم","example":"What size are your shoes?","image_id":"GV-L02-U5-LS3-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U5-LS3-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"Some clothes come in pairs because they have two parts: a pair of shoes, a pair of socks, a pair of sneakers, a pair of pants (US), a pair of gloves.\nShopping words: price (how much it costs), size (S, M, L), cheap ↔ expensive.\nPhrasal verbs for clothes: try on (wear to check the size in a shop), put on (start wearing), take off (stop wearing). With it/them, the pronoun goes in the middle: Try it on. Take them off.\nCollocations/phrases: a pair of: shoes • sneakers • socks • gloves • pants (US) • sunglasses | cheap ↔ expensive • small ↔ large • tight ↔ loose | try on • put on • take off → Try it on. Put them on. Take it off.","examples":["I need a new pair of socks.","This thobe is the right size.","The price of the cap is 25 riyals.","These sandals are cheap – only 20 riyals!","The gold watch is very expensive.","Try on the jacket before you buy it.","Take off your shoes at the door.","Put on your scarf; it's cold."],"common_errors":["✗ I need a socks. → ✓ I need a pair of socks. (Socks come in pairs.)","✗ Try on it. → ✓ Try it on. (Pronouns go in the middle: try it on.)","✗ This shirt is very cheap price. → ✓ This shirt is very cheap. / The price is low. (cheap describes the thing.)","✗ I wear my shoes when I go out. (start) → ✓ I put on my shoes when I go out. (put on = start wearing.)"],"arabic":"بعض الملابس نقول معها a pair of لأنها من جزأين: a pair of shoes (زوج أحذية).\ncheap (رخيص) ↔ expensive (غالٍ)، price (السعر)، size (المقاس).\ntry on (يقيس)، put on (يلبس)، take off (يخلع)، والضمير يأتي في الوسط: Try it on."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “What to Wear: Clothes and Shopping Words”. Let’s learn clothes words; a pair of…; cheap ↔ expensive; put on / take off / try on together.","on_screen":"GV-L02-U5-LS3 | What to Wear: Clothes and Shopping Words","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Meet some new words. price: how much money something costs. cheap: not costing a lot of money. expensive: costing a lot of money.","on_screen":"price | cheap | expensive","visual":"Each word card flips over to show its picture (vocabulary image briefs) and Arabic meaning."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Some clothes come in pairs because they have two parts: a pair of shoes, a pair of socks, a pair of sneakers, a pair of pants (US), a pair of gloves. Shopping words: price (how much it costs), size (S, M, L), cheap ↔ expensive.","on_screen":"clothes words; a pair of…; cheap ↔ expensive; put on / take off / try on","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. I need a new pair of socks. This thobe is the right size. The price of the cap is 25 riyals.","on_screen":"I need a new pair of socks. / This thobe is the right size. / The price of the cap is 25 riyals.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “I need a socks.” That’s not right. We say: “I need a pair of socks.” Socks come in pairs.","on_screen":"✗ I need a socks.   ✓ I need a pair of socks.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: Do we say \"a socks\" or \"a pair of socks\"? … Think! … *a pair of socks*. Great job! Now you can say: I can name clothes and say \"a pair of socks\".","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can name clothes and say \"a pair of socks\".","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: clothes words; a pair of…; cheap ↔ expensive; put on / take off / try on.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","بعض الملابس نقول معها a pair of لأنها من جزأين: a pair of shoes (زوج أحذية).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: I need a socks. — الصحيح: I need a pair of socks.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أسمّي الملابس وأقول a pair of socks."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS3-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","items":[{"q":"I need ___ gloves for winter.","options":["a pair of","a","an","one"],"answer":"a pair of","explanation":"Two-part clothes → a pair of.","explanation_ar":"الملابس ذات الجزأين ← a pair of."},{"q":"This watch costs 2,000 riyals. It's ___.","options":["loose","small","cheap","expensive"],"answer":"expensive","explanation":"cheap ↔ expensive; small ↔ large.","explanation_ar":"الأضداد."},{"q":"Men in Saudi Arabia often wear a white ___.","options":["sock","dress","thobe","scarf"],"answer":"thobe","explanation":"Choose the right clothes or shopping word.","explanation_ar":"اختر كلمة الملابس أو التسوّق المناسبة."},{"q":"These shoes are too small. Do you have a bigger ___?","options":["pair","size","price","cap"],"answer":"size","explanation":"Choose the right clothes or shopping word.","explanation_ar":"اختر كلمة الملابس أو التسوّق المناسبة."},{"q":"Can I try this shirt ___?","options":["in","on","at","off"],"answer":"on","explanation":"try on / put on / take off – pronoun in the middle (try it on).","explanation_ar":"الضمير في الوسط."},{"q":"It's hot in here. ___ your jacket.","options":["Take off","Try on","Take on","Put on"],"answer":"Take off","explanation":"try on / put on / take off – pronoun in the middle (try it on).","explanation_ar":"الضمير في الوسط."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS3-B1","type":"match","instructions":"Guided practice: Match the clothes to the body part.","items":[{"q":"cap","options":["neck","head","hands","eyes","feet, for sports","feet"],"answer":"head","explanation":"cap → head. Two-part clothes → a pair of.","explanation_ar":"الملابس ذات الجزأين ← a pair of."},{"q":"scarf","options":["neck","head","hands","eyes","feet, for sports","feet"],"answer":"neck","explanation":"scarf → neck. Two-part clothes → a pair of.","explanation_ar":"الملابس ذات الجزأين ← a pair of."},{"q":"socks","options":["neck","head","hands","eyes","feet, for sports","feet"],"answer":"feet","explanation":"socks → feet. Two-part clothes → a pair of.","explanation_ar":"الملابس ذات الجزأين ← a pair of."},{"q":"gloves","options":["neck","head","hands","eyes","feet, for sports","feet"],"answer":"hands","explanation":"gloves → hands. Two-part clothes → a pair of.","explanation_ar":"الملابس ذات الجزأين ← a pair of."},{"q":"sunglasses","options":["neck","head","hands","eyes","feet, for sports","feet"],"answer":"eyes","explanation":"sunglasses → eyes. Two-part clothes → a pair of.","explanation_ar":"الملابس ذات الجزأين ← a pair of."},{"q":"sneakers","options":["neck","head","hands","eyes","feet, for sports","feet"],"answer":"feet, for sports","explanation":"sneakers → feet, for sports. Two-part clothes → a pair of.","explanation_ar":"الملابس ذات الجزأين ← a pair of."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS3-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Write about your clothes.","items":[{"q":"At school, I wear ___.","options":[],"answer":"At school, I wear a white thobe.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses clothes words; a pair of…; cheap ↔ expensive; put on / take off / try on correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"When it's cold, I put on ___.","options":[],"answer":"When it's cold, I put on a jacket.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses clothes words; a pair of…; cheap ↔ expensive; put on / take off / try on correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"I take off my shoes when ___.","options":[],"answer":"I take off my shoes when I enter the mosque.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses clothes words; a pair of…; cheap ↔ expensive; put on / take off / try on correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"My favorite clothes are ___.","options":[],"answer":"My favorite clothes are my blue sneakers.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses clothes words; a pair of…; cheap ↔ expensive; put on / take off / try on correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Something cheap I want to buy: ___.","options":[],"answer":"a new cap","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses clothes words; a pair of…; cheap ↔ expensive; put on / take off / try on correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS3-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Design a school uniform.","items":[{"q":"Draw a uniform for your school. Label 4 pieces of clothing.","options":[],"answer":"white thobe, gray jacket, black shoes, gray socks","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses clothes words; a pair of…; cheap ↔ expensive; put on / take off / try on correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 3 sentences about it with colors and a pair of.","options":[],"answer":"The thobe is white. The jacket is gray. Students wear a pair of black shoes.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses clothes words; a pair of…; cheap ↔ expensive; put on / take off / try on correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence with try on, one with put on and one with take off.","options":[],"answer":"Try on the jacket. Put on your shoes. Take off your cap in class.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses clothes words; a pair of…; cheap ↔ expensive; put on / take off / try on correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Word Dominoes","mechanic":"matching","rules":["Deal the dominoes equally in teams of four.","Player 1 places a domino; the next player adds a domino whose word matches the open definition.","If you cannot play, pass.","The first player with no dominoes left wins."],"data":[{"word":"shirt","match":"a piece of clothing for the top of your body, with buttons","arabic":"قميص"},{"word":"thobe","match":"a long robe that men and boys wear in Saudi Arabia","arabic":"ثوب"},{"word":"dress","match":"a piece of clothing for girls and women, from the shoulders down","arabic":"فستان"},{"word":"shoes","match":"things you wear on your feet when you go out","arabic":"حذاء"},{"word":"sneakers","match":"soft sports shoes (American English)","arabic":"حذاء رياضي"},{"word":"socks","match":"soft things you wear on your feet inside shoes","arabic":"جوارب"},{"word":"cap","match":"a soft hat with a hard part at the front","arabic":"قبعة (كاب)"},{"word":"scarf","match":"a long piece of cloth you wear around your neck","arabic":"وشاح"},{"word":"price","match":"how much money something costs","arabic":"سعر"},{"word":"cheap","match":"not costing a lot of money","arabic":"رخيص"},{"word":"expensive","match":"costing a lot of money","arabic":"غالٍ"},{"word":"size","match":"how big or small something is","arabic":"مقاس / حجم"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"I want ___ sunglasses.","options":["a pair of","one","an","a"],"answer":"a pair of","explanation":"Two-part clothes → a pair of.","explanation_ar":"الملابس ذات الجزأين ← a pair of."},{"q":"This scarf is only 5 riyals. It's ___.","options":["large","expensive","cheap","tight"],"answer":"cheap","explanation":"cheap ↔ expensive; small ↔ large.","explanation_ar":"الأضداد."},{"q":"Girls often wear a long ___ to the party.","options":["sock","cap","thobe","dress"],"answer":"dress","explanation":"Choose the right clothes or shopping word.","explanation_ar":"اختر كلمة الملابس أو التسوّق المناسبة."},{"q":"The ___ of the shoes is 90 riyals.","options":["color","price","pair","size"],"answer":"price","explanation":"Choose the right clothes or shopping word.","explanation_ar":"اختر كلمة الملابس أو التسوّق المناسبة."},{"q":"","options":["Take off it your shoes, please.","Take off your shoes off, please.","Take your shoes, please off.","Take your shoes off, please."],"answer":"Take your shoes off, please.","explanation":"try on / put on / take off – pronoun in the middle (try it on).","explanation_ar":"الضمير في الوسط."},{"q":"","options":["I like this cap. Can I try it in?","I like this cap. Can I try on?","I like this cap. Can I try on it?","I like this cap. Can I try it on?"],"answer":"I like this cap. Can I try it on?","explanation":"try on / put on / take off – pronoun in the middle (try it on).","explanation_ar":"الضمير في الوسط."},{"q":"small ↔ ___","options":["tight","large","cheap","short"],"answer":"large","explanation":"cheap ↔ expensive; small ↔ large.","explanation_ar":"الأضداد."},{"q":"We wear ___ on our feet inside our shoes.","options":["caps","scarves","socks","gloves"],"answer":"socks","explanation":"Choose the right clothes or shopping word.","explanation_ar":"اختر كلمة الملابس أو التسوّق المناسبة."},{"q":"Put ___ your coat. It's freezing!","options":["on","off","in","at"],"answer":"on","explanation":"try on / put on / take off – pronoun in the middle (try it on).","explanation_ar":"الضمير في الوسط."},{"q":"What ___ are your shoes? – 38.","options":["pair","size","price","cost"],"answer":"size","explanation":"Choose the right clothes or shopping word.","explanation_ar":"اختر كلمة الملابس أو التسوّق المناسبة."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS3-IMG01","prompt":"A clothes shop with labeled racks: thobes, dresses, scarves, caps, socks and sneakers; size signs S, M, L and price tags showing cheap and expensive. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A clothes shop with labeled racks: thobes, dresses, scarves, caps, socks and sneakers; size signs S, M, L and price tags showing cheap and expensive"},{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS3-IMG02","prompt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 4 small picture icons of the lesson words; empty labels. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 4 small picture icons of the lesson words"},{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS3-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows price (how much money something costs); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing price: how much money something costs"},{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS3-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows cheap (not costing a lot of money); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing cheap: not costing a lot of money"},{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS3-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows expensive (costing a lot of money); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing expensive: costing a lot of money"},{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS3-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows size (how big or small something is); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing size: how big or small something is"},{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS3-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Word Dominoes”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Word Dominoes"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U5-LS3-W01","script":"price. price. The price is on the label.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U5-LS3-W02","script":"cheap. cheap. This T-shirt is cheap.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U5-LS3-W03","script":"expensive. expensive. Gold watches are very expensive.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U5-LS3-W04","script":"size. size. What size are your shoes?","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U5-LS3-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “What to Wear: Clothes and Shopping Words”. Let’s learn clothes words; a pair of…; cheap ↔ expensive; put on / take off / try on together. Meet some new words. price: how much money something costs. cheap: not costing a lot of money. expensive: costing a lot of money. Some clothes come in pairs because they have two parts: a pair of shoes, a pair of socks, a pair of sneakers, a pair of pants (US), a pair of gloves. Shopping words: price (how much it costs), size (S, M, L), cheap ↔ expensive. Here are some examples. I need a new pair of socks. This thobe is the right size. The price of the cap is 25 riyals. Be careful! Some learners say: “I need a socks.” That’s not right. We say: “I need a pair of socks.” Socks come in pairs. Quick check: Do we say \"a socks\" or \"a pair of socks\"? … Think! … *a pair of socks*. Great job! Now you can say: I can name clothes and say \"a pair of socks\".","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS4","title":"Don't, It's, They're: Apostrophes in Contractions","objectives":["Students will be able to write common contractions with an apostrophe in the right place.","Students will be able to tell it's (it is) from its (belongs to it).","I can write \"don't\", \"it's\" and \"they're\" correctly.","I can choose between it's and its."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة الاختصارات الشائعة مع وضع الفاصلة العلوية في مكانها الصحيح.","سيتمكن الطلاب من التمييز بين it's وits.","أستطيع أن أكتب don't وit's وthey're بشكل صحيح.","أستطيع أن أختار بين it's وits."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"shirt","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ʃɝt/","definition":"a piece of clothing for the top of your body, with buttons","arabic":"قميص","example":"His school shirt is white.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"thobe","pos":"noun","ipa":"/θoʊb/","definition":"a long robe that men and boys wear in Saudi Arabia","arabic":"ثوب","example":"Dad wears a white thobe on Friday.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"dress","pos":"noun","ipa":"/drɛs/","definition":"a piece of clothing for girls and women, from the shoulders down","arabic":"فستان","example":"Lina's dress is long and green.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"shoes","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ʃuz/","definition":"things you wear on your feet when you go out","arabic":"حذاء","example":"Put your shoes by the door.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"sneakers","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈsnikɚz/","definition":"soft sports shoes (American English)","arabic":"حذاء رياضي","example":"My sneakers are good for running.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"socks","pos":"noun","ipa":"/sɑks/","definition":"soft things you wear on your feet inside shoes","arabic":"جوارب","example":"These socks keep my feet warm.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"A contraction is a short form of two words. The apostrophe (') takes the place of the missing letter(s): do not → don't, I am → I'm.\nCommon contractions: I'm, you're, he's, she's, it's, we're, they're, isn't, aren't, don't, doesn't, can't.\nit's = it is (It's cheap). its = belongs to it (The shop has its own café). No apostrophe for its!\nThe apostrophe goes where letters are missing: is not → isn't\nDon't put the apostrophe between the wrong letters: (not: do'nt) → don't\nit's = it is / it has • its = belongs to it\nthey're = they are (not their or there)","examples":["I'm looking for a blue cap.","It's too expensive.","These shoes aren't my size.","My brother doesn't like shopping.","They're on sale today!","The shop isn't open on Friday morning.","We don't need new socks.","The bag has its price on a small tag."],"common_errors":["✗ dont → ✓ don't (Put the apostrophe where the o is missing.)","✗ does'nt → ✓ doesn't (The apostrophe replaces the o in not.)","✗ Its cheap. → ✓ It's cheap. (it's = it is.)","✗ The cat licks it's paw. → ✓ The cat licks its paw. (its = belongs to it.)"],"arabic":"الاختصار كلمتان قصيرتان، والفاصلة العلوية (') مكان الحرف المحذوف: do not → don't.\nالفاصلة العلوية مكان الحرف المحذوف بالضبط: doesn't وليس does'nt.\nit's = it is، أما its فتعني «له/لها» لغير العاقل وبدون فاصلة علوية."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Don't, It's, They're: Apostrophes in Contractions”. Let’s learn apostrophes in contractions (I'm, it's, don't, doesn't, isn't, aren't, they're, can't) together.","on_screen":"GV-L02-U5-LS4 | Don't, It's, They're: Apostrophes in Contractions","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"A contraction is a short form of two words. The apostrophe (') takes the place of the missing letter(s): do not → don't, I am → I'm.","on_screen":"apostrophes in contractions (I'm, it's, don't, doesn't, isn't, aren't, they're, can't)","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"A contraction is a short form of two words. The apostrophe (') takes the place of the missing letter(s): do not → don't, I am → I'm. Common contractions: I'm, you're, he's, she's, it's, we're, they're, isn't, aren't, don't, doesn't, can't.","on_screen":"The apostrophe goes where letters are missing: is not → isn't • Don't put the apostrophe between the wrong letters: (not: do'nt) → don't • it's = it is / it has • its = belongs to it","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. I'm looking for a blue cap. It's too expensive. These shoes aren't my size.","on_screen":"I'm looking for a blue cap. / It's too expensive. / These shoes aren't my size.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “dont.” That’s not right. We say: “don't.” Put the apostrophe where the o is missing.","on_screen":"✗ dont   ✓ don't","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: What letter does the apostrophe replace in \"isn't\"? … Think! … The *o* in not. Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"don't\", \"it's\" and \"they're\" correctly.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can write \"don't\", \"it's\" and \"they're\" correctly.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: apostrophes in contractions (I'm, it's, don't, doesn't, isn't, aren't, they're, can't).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","الاختصار كلمتان قصيرتان، والفاصلة العلوية (') مكان الحرف المحذوف: do not → don't.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: dont — الصحيح: don't","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أكتب don't وit's وthey're بشكل صحيح."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Big Sale! (editing passage)","body":"Were having a big sale today! Its all half price. Shoes arent expensive here. Our shop opens it's doors at nine. Hurry – the sale doesnt last long!","word_count":28,"audio_id":""}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS4-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct contraction.","items":[{"q":"do not → ___","options":["don't","do'nt","don't'","dont"],"answer":"don't","explanation":"The apostrophe replaces the missing letter(s).","explanation_ar":"الفاصلة العلوية مكان الحرف المحذوف."},{"q":"is not → ___","options":["isn't","is'nt","i'snt","isnt"],"answer":"isn't","explanation":"Put the apostrophe exactly where the letter is missing.","explanation_ar":"ضع الفاصلة في مكانها الصحيح."},{"q":"they are → ___","options":["there","their","theyr'e","they're"],"answer":"they're","explanation":"they're = they are.","explanation_ar":"they're تعني they are."},{"q":"does not → ___","options":["does'nt","doe'snt","doesn't","doesnt"],"answer":"doesn't","explanation":"Put the apostrophe exactly where the letter is missing.","explanation_ar":"ضع الفاصلة في مكانها الصحيح."},{"q":"___ a nice shop. (It is)","options":["It is'","It's","Its'","Its"],"answer":"It's","explanation":"it's = it is; its = belongs to it.","explanation_ar":"it's تعني it is وits للملكية."},{"q":"The shop changed ___ name. (belongs to it)","options":["its'","it is","its","it's"],"answer":"its","explanation":"it's = it is; its = belongs to it.","explanation_ar":"it's تعني it is وits للملكية."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS4-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Write the contraction.","items":[{"q":"I am buying a scarf.  (contraction)","options":[],"answer":"I'm buying a scarf.","explanation":"The apostrophe replaces the missing letter(s).","explanation_ar":"الفاصلة العلوية مكان الحرف المحذوف."},{"q":"We are not ready.  (contraction)","options":[],"answer":"We aren't ready.","explanation":"The apostrophe replaces the missing letter(s).","explanation_ar":"الفاصلة العلوية مكان الحرف المحذوف."},{"q":"She does not wear a cap.  (contraction)","options":[],"answer":"She doesn't wear a cap.","explanation":"Put the apostrophe exactly where the letter is missing.","explanation_ar":"ضع الفاصلة في مكانها الصحيح."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS4-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Correct the mistake.","items":[{"q":"These socks arent clean.","options":[],"answer":"These socks aren't clean.","explanation":"arent → aren't. The apostrophe replaces the missing letter(s).","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: arent → aren't. الفاصلة العلوية مكان الحرف المحذوف."},{"q":"Its raining, so take a jacket.","options":[],"answer":"It's raining, so take a jacket.","explanation":"Its → It's. it's = it is; its = belongs to it.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: Its → It's. it's تعني it is وits للملكية."},{"q":"My dad does'nt like long queues.","options":[],"answer":"My dad doesn't like long queues.","explanation":"does'nt → doesn't. Put the apostrophe exactly where the letter is missing.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: does'nt → doesn't. ضع الفاصلة في مكانها الصحيح."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS4-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Edit the shop sign.","items":[{"q":"Were having a big sale today! It's all half price.","options":[],"answer":"We're having a big sale today! It's all half price.","explanation":"Were → We're. The apostrophe replaces the missing letter(s).","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: Were → We're. الفاصلة العلوية مكان الحرف المحذوف."},{"q":"We're having a big sale today! Its all half price.","options":[],"answer":"We're having a big sale today! It's all half price.","explanation":"Its → It's. The apostrophe replaces the missing letter(s).","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: Its → It's. الفاصلة العلوية مكان الحرف المحذوف."},{"q":"Shoes arent expensive here.","options":[],"answer":"Shoes aren't expensive here.","explanation":"arent → aren't. The apostrophe replaces the missing letter(s).","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: arent → aren't. الفاصلة العلوية مكان الحرف المحذوف."},{"q":"Our shop opens it's doors at nine.","options":[],"answer":"Our shop opens its doors at nine.","explanation":"it's → its. The apostrophe replaces the missing letter(s).","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: it's → its. الفاصلة العلوية مكان الحرف المحذوف."},{"q":"Hurry – the sale doesnt last long!","options":[],"answer":"Hurry – the sale doesn't last long!","explanation":"doesnt → doesn't. The apostrophe replaces the missing letter(s).","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: doesnt → doesn't. الفاصلة العلوية مكان الحرف المحذوف."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS4-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write with contractions.","items":[{"q":"Write 3 sentences about shopping with I'm, don't and it's.","options":[],"answer":"I'm at the mall. I don't like big crowds. It's very busy today.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses apostrophes in contractions (I'm, it's, don't, doesn't, isn't, aren't, they're, can't) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence with it's and one with its.","options":[],"answer":"It's a great shop. The shop has its own parking lot.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses apostrophes in contractions (I'm, it's, don't, doesn't, isn't, aren't, they're, can't) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Find 2 contractions in a book. Write them and the full words.","options":[],"answer":"can't = cannot; she's = she is","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses apostrophes in contractions (I'm, it's, don't, doesn't, isn't, aren't, they're, can't) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Speed Spell","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["The teacher says a word and a short sentence with it.","Students write the word in 10 seconds.","Show boards on \"Show me!\". Correct = 1 point.","After 10 words, partners check each other's boards and correct any mistakes."],"data":[{"word":"don't","clue":""},{"word":"doesn't","clue":""},{"word":"isn't","clue":""},{"word":"aren't","clue":""},{"word":"it's","clue":""},{"word":"they're","clue":""},{"word":"I'm","clue":""},{"word":"can't","clue":""},{"word":"shirt","clue":"a piece of clothing for the top of your body, with buttons"},{"word":"thobe","clue":"a long robe that men and boys wear in Saudi Arabia"},{"word":"dress","clue":"a piece of clothing for girls and women, from the shoulders down"},{"word":"shoes","clue":"things you wear on your feet when you go out"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"are not → ___","options":["are'nt","arent","ar'ent","aren't"],"answer":"aren't","explanation":"The apostrophe replaces the missing letter(s).","explanation_ar":"الفاصلة العلوية مكان الحرف المحذوف."},{"q":"I am → ___","options":["I m","I'm","Im","I'am"],"answer":"I'm","explanation":"The apostrophe replaces the missing letter(s).","explanation_ar":"الفاصلة العلوية مكان الحرف المحذوف."},{"q":"","options":["My sister doe'snt like pink.","My sister does'nt like pink.","My sister doesn't like pink.","My sister doesnt like pink."],"answer":"My sister doesn't like pink.","explanation":"Put the apostrophe exactly where the letter is missing.","explanation_ar":"ضع الفاصلة في مكانها الصحيح."},{"q":"","options":["Its a beautiful dress.","Its' a beautiful dress.","It's a beautiful dress.","It's' a beautiful dress."],"answer":"It's a beautiful dress.","explanation":"it's = it is; its = belongs to it.","explanation_ar":"it's تعني it is وits للملكية."},{"q":"","options":["The bird is building it is nest.","The bird is building its' nest.","The bird is building it's nest.","The bird is building its nest."],"answer":"The bird is building its nest.","explanation":"it's = it is; its = belongs to it.","explanation_ar":"it's تعني it is وits للملكية."},{"q":"","options":["Their buying new uniforms.","There buying new uniforms.","Theyr'e buying new uniforms.","They're buying new uniforms."],"answer":"They're buying new uniforms.","explanation":"they're = they are.","explanation_ar":"they're تعني they are."},{"q":"Which word needs an apostrophe?","options":["cant","hats","cats","caps"],"answer":"cant","explanation":"The apostrophe replaces the missing letter(s).","explanation_ar":"الفاصلة العلوية مكان الحرف المحذوف."},{"q":"","options":["We don't need a bag, thanks.","We dont need a bag, thanks.","We don't' need a bag, thanks.","We do'nt need a bag, thanks."],"answer":"We don't need a bag, thanks.","explanation":"The apostrophe replaces the missing letter(s).","explanation_ar":"الفاصلة العلوية مكان الحرف المحذوف."},{"q":"you are → ___","options":["youre","you're","you'are","your"],"answer":"you're","explanation":"The apostrophe replaces the missing letter(s).","explanation_ar":"الفاصلة العلوية مكان الحرف المحذوف."},{"q":"","options":["The shoes aren't in the box.","The shoes ar'ent in the box.","The shoes are'nt in the box.","The shoes arent in the box."],"answer":"The shoes aren't in the box.","explanation":"Put the apostrophe exactly where the letter is missing.","explanation_ar":"ضع الفاصلة في مكانها الصحيح."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS4-IMG01","prompt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Clothes and Shopping” that shows apostrophes in contractions (I'm, it's, don't, doesn't, isn't, aren't, they're, can't) in action. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Clothes and Shopping” that shows apostrophes in contractions (I'm, it's, don't, doesn't, isn't, aren't, they're, can't) in action"},{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS4-IMG02","prompt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen"},{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS4-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Speed Spell”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Speed Spell"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U5-LS4-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Don't, It's, They're: Apostrophes in Contractions”. Let’s learn apostrophes in contractions (I'm, it's, don't, doesn't, isn't, aren't, they're, can't) together. A contraction is a short form of two words. The apostrophe (') takes the place of the missing letter(s): do not → don't, I am → I'm. A contraction is a short form of two words. The apostrophe (') takes the place of the missing letter(s): do not → don't, I am → I'm. Common contractions: I'm, you're, he's, she's, it's, we're, they're, isn't, aren't, don't, doesn't, can't. Here are some examples. I'm looking for a blue cap. It's too expensive. These shoes aren't my size. Be careful! Some learners say: “dont.” That’s not right. We say: “don't.” Put the apostrophe where the o is missing. Quick check: What letter does the apostrophe replace in \"isn't\"? … Think! … The *o* in not. Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"don't\", \"it's\" and \"they're\" correctly.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS5","title":"At the Market: Language in Use","objectives":["Students will be able to role-play buying clothes at a market.","Students will be able to write a shopping dialogue with prices, object pronouns and contractions.","I can buy clothes in English.","I can write a shopping dialogue."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من تمثيل شراء الملابس في السوق.","سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة حوار تسوّق مع الأسعار وضمائر المفعول والاختصارات.","أستطيع أن أشتري الملابس بالإنجليزية.","أستطيع أن أكتب حوار تسوّق."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"shirt","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ʃɝt/","definition":"a piece of clothing for the top of your body, with buttons","arabic":"قميص","example":"His school shirt is white.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"thobe","pos":"noun","ipa":"/θoʊb/","definition":"a long robe that men and boys wear in Saudi Arabia","arabic":"ثوب","example":"Dad wears a white thobe on Friday.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"dress","pos":"noun","ipa":"/drɛs/","definition":"a piece of clothing for girls and women, from the shoulders down","arabic":"فستان","example":"Lina's dress is long and green.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"shoes","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ʃuz/","definition":"things you wear on your feet when you go out","arabic":"حذاء","example":"Put your shoes by the door.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"sneakers","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈsnikɚz/","definition":"soft sports shoes (American English)","arabic":"حذاء رياضي","example":"My sneakers are good for running.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"socks","pos":"noun","ipa":"/sɑks/","definition":"soft things you wear on your feet inside shoes","arabic":"جوارب","example":"These socks keep my feet warm.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"cap","pos":"noun","ipa":"/kæp/","definition":"a soft hat with a hard part at the front","arabic":"قبعة (كاب)","example":"Adam wears his cap backward.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"scarf","pos":"noun","ipa":"/skɑrf/","definition":"a long piece of cloth you wear around your neck","arabic":"وشاح","example":"Grandma knits a red scarf.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"price","pos":"noun","ipa":"/praɪs/","definition":"how much money something costs","arabic":"سعر","example":"The price is on the label.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"cheap","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/tʃip/","definition":"not costing a lot of money","arabic":"رخيص","example":"This T-shirt is cheap.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"expensive","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ɪkˈspɛnsɪv/","definition":"costing a lot of money","arabic":"غالٍ","example":"Gold watches are very expensive.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"size","pos":"noun","ipa":"/saɪz/","definition":"how big or small something is","arabic":"مقاس / حجم","example":"What size are your shoes?","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Today you use all of Unit 5: object pronouns, How much is/are…?, How many…?, clothes words, a pair of, phrasal verbs and contractions.\nA shopping dialogue is polite: start with Excuse me, ask about the price and size, and say Thank you.\n✔ object pronouns: Can I try it on? I'll take them.\n✔ How much is this…? / How much are these…?\n✔ clothes words and a pair of\n✔ contractions with apostrophes: it's, they're, don't","examples":["How much are these sneakers?","They're 130 riyals.","Can I try them on?","It's the wrong size for me.","Do you have it in medium?","I don't need a pair of gloves today.","How many scarves do you want? – Two, please.","This cap is for my brother. I'll give it to him."],"common_errors":["✗ How much this cap? → ✓ How much is this cap? (Don't forget is.)","✗ Can I try on them? → ✓ Can I try them on? (Pronoun in the middle.)","✗ Its too big for I. → ✓ It's too big for me. (it's = it is; after for → me.)"],"arabic":"نراجع ضمائر المفعول وأسئلة الأسعار وكلمات الملابس والاختصارات.\nفي التسوّق: نبدأ بـ Excuse me، ونسأل عن السعر والمقاس، ونشكر في النهاية.\nتذكّر: Can I try it on? والضمير في الوسط."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “At the Market: Language in Use”. Let’s learn object pronouns, prices with How much/How many, clothes words and contractions (unit review) together.","on_screen":"GV-L02-U5-LS5 | At the Market: Language in Use","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Market day: half the class are sellers with price cards, half are shoppers with 100 pretend riyals. Shoppers ask \"How much is/are…? Can I try it on? Do you have it in…?\" and buy two things.","on_screen":"Language in use","visual":"Split screen: two cast members talking, with speech bubbles appearing."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Today you use all of Unit 5: object pronouns, How much is/are…?, How many…?, clothes words, a pair of, phrasal verbs and contractions. A shopping dialogue is polite: start with Excuse me, ask about the price and size, and say Thank you.","on_screen":"✔ object pronouns: Can I try it on? I'll take them. • ✔ How much is this…? / How much are these…? • ✔ clothes words and a pair of","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. How much are these sneakers? They're 130 riyals. Can I try them on?","on_screen":"How much are these sneakers? / They're 130 riyals. / Can I try them on?","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “How much this cap?.” That’s not right. We say: “How much is this cap?.” Don't forget is.","on_screen":"✗ How much this cap?   ✓ How much is this cap?","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: what is wrong with “Can I try on them?”? … Think! … It should be “Can I try them on?”. Great job! Now you can say: I can buy clothes in English.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can buy clothes in English.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: object pronouns, prices with How much/How many, clothes words and contractions (unit review).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نراجع ضمائر المفعول وأسئلة الأسعار وكلمات الملابس والاختصارات.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: How much this cap? — الصحيح: How much is this cap?","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أشتري الملابس بالإنجليزية."]},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"Buying a Scarf – Sara","body":"Sara: Excuse me, how much is this scarf?\nSeller: It's 40 riyals.\nSara: It's lovely, but it's a little expensive. How much are those scarves?\nSeller: They're 25 riyals each.\nSara: I like the green one. Can I see it, please?\nSeller: Of course. Here you are.\nSara: Thanks! I'll take it. It's for my grandma – she'll love it!","word_count":60,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U5-LS5-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS5-A1","type":"true_false","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read the dialogue. True or False?","items":[{"q":"The first scarf is 40 riyals.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Buying a Scarf – Sara”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Sara thinks the first scarf is cheap.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “Buying a Scarf – Sara”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"The other scarves are 25 riyals each.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Buying a Scarf – Sara”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Sara chooses a blue scarf.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “Buying a Scarf – Sara”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"The scarf is a gift for Sara's grandma.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Buying a Scarf – Sara”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"The seller doesn't show Sara the green scarf.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “Buying a Scarf – Sara”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS5-B1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Guided practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"Sara likes the green scarf. She buys ___.","options":["her","them","its","it"],"answer":"it","explanation":"Object pronoun after a verb or preposition (me, him, her, it, us, them).","explanation_ar":"ضمير المفعول بعد الفعل أو حرف الجر."},{"q":"How much ___ those scarves?","options":["do","are","does","is"],"answer":"are","explanation":"How much is (one) / are (many)…?","explanation_ar":"How much is للمفرد وare للجمع."},{"q":"It's a gift for Grandma. Sara gives it to ___.","options":["hers","him","she","her"],"answer":"her","explanation":"Object pronoun after a verb or preposition (me, him, her, it, us, them).","explanation_ar":"ضمير المفعول بعد الفعل أو حرف الجر."},{"q":"","options":["Its a little expensive.","Its' a little expensive.","It's a little expensive.","It's' a little expensive."],"answer":"It's a little expensive.","explanation":"Apostrophe where letters are missing.","explanation_ar":"الفاصلة العلوية مكان الحرف المحذوف."},{"q":"I need ___ new socks for school.","options":["a pair of","a","an","one"],"answer":"a pair of","explanation":"Choose the right clothes or shopping word.","explanation_ar":"اختر كلمة الملابس المناسبة."},{"q":"","options":["This jacket is nice. Can I try it on?","This jacket is nice. Can I try it in?","This jacket is nice. Can try I it on?","This jacket is nice. Can I try on it?"],"answer":"This jacket is nice. Can I try it on?","explanation":"Pronoun goes in the middle: try it on.","explanation_ar":"الضمير في الوسط."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS5-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Market day. Write what you say.","items":[{"q":"Ask the price of one thing.","options":[],"answer":"How much is this cap?","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses object pronouns, prices with How much/How many, clothes words and contractions (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Ask the price of two things.","options":[],"answer":"How much are these socks?","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses object pronouns, prices with How much/How many, clothes words and contractions (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Ask to try something on.","options":[],"answer":"Can I try it on, please?","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses object pronouns, prices with How much/How many, clothes words and contractions (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Say it's the wrong size.","options":[],"answer":"It's too small for me.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses object pronouns, prices with How much/How many, clothes words and contractions (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Say what you buy and who it's for.","options":[],"answer":"I'll take it. It's for my brother – I'll give it to him.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses object pronouns, prices with How much/How many, clothes words and contractions (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS5-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write a shopping dialogue.","items":[{"q":"Plan: what you buy, the prices and who it is for.","options":[],"answer":"sneakers – 120 riyals – for me; scarf – 30 riyals – for my mom","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses object pronouns, prices with How much/How many, clothes words and contractions (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a 6–8 line dialogue.","options":[],"answer":"A: Excuse me, how much are these sneakers? B: They're 120 riyals. A: Can I try them on? B: Sure. A: They're perfect! I'll take them. B: Thank you!","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses object pronouns, prices with How much/How many, clothes words and contractions (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Check: object pronouns? is/are? apostrophes? Fix one mistake.","options":[],"answer":"I changed \"Its perfect\" to \"It's perfect\".","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses object pronouns, prices with How much/How many, clothes words and contractions (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Spin the Review Wheel","mechanic":"spin_wheel","rules":["A player spins the wheel and lands on a word.","Say what the word means and use it in a sentence with object pronouns, prices with How much/How many, clothes words and contractions (unit review).","Teammates check: meaning (1 point), grammar (1 point), pronunciation (1 point).","Highest total after 6 minutes wins."],"data":[{"cue":"shirt","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"thobe","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"dress","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"shoes","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"sneakers","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"socks","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"cap","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"scarf","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"price","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"cheap","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"expensive","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"size","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"These sandals are cheap. I'll buy ___.","options":["it","their","they","them"],"answer":"them","explanation":"Object pronoun after a verb or preposition (me, him, her, it, us, them).","explanation_ar":"ضمير المفعول بعد الفعل أو حرف الجر."},{"q":"How much ___ that thobe?","options":["are","do","is","does"],"answer":"is","explanation":"How much is (one) / are (many)…?","explanation_ar":"How much is للمفرد وare للجمع."},{"q":"Grandpa needs a new cap. Let's get one for ___.","options":["him","them","he","his"],"answer":"him","explanation":"Object pronoun after a verb or preposition (me, him, her, it, us, them).","explanation_ar":"ضمير المفعول بعد الفعل أو حرف الجر."},{"q":"","options":["There 50 riyals each.","Their 50 riyals each.","They're 50 riyals each.","Theyre 50 riyals each."],"answer":"They're 50 riyals each.","explanation":"Apostrophe where letters are missing.","explanation_ar":"الفاصلة العلوية مكان الحرف المحذوف."},{"q":"This scarf costs 500 riyals. It's ___.","options":["loose","small","cheap","expensive"],"answer":"expensive","explanation":"Choose the right clothes or shopping word.","explanation_ar":"اختر كلمة الملابس المناسبة."},{"q":"","options":["Take off it your cap in the mosque.","Take off your cap in the mosque.","Take your cap off in the mosque off.","Take in your cap off the mosque."],"answer":"Take off your cap in the mosque.","explanation":"Pronoun goes in the middle: try it on.","explanation_ar":"الضمير في الوسط."},{"q":"How ___ pairs of socks do you want?","options":["big","much","long","many"],"answer":"many","explanation":"How much is (one) / are (many)…?","explanation_ar":"How much is للمفرد وare للجمع."},{"q":"","options":["The shop isnt open on Friday morning.","The shop isn't' open on Friday morning.","The shop isn't open on Friday morning.","The shop is'nt open on Friday morning."],"answer":"The shop isn't open on Friday morning.","explanation":"Apostrophe where letters are missing.","explanation_ar":"الفاصلة العلوية مكان الحرف المحذوف."},{"q":"Can you help ___? We need a bigger size.","options":["us","we","our","ours"],"answer":"us","explanation":"Object pronoun after a verb or preposition (me, him, her, it, us, them).","explanation_ar":"ضمير المفعول بعد الفعل أو حرف الجر."},{"q":"Choose the best line for a seller:","options":["They 40 riyals. You want try them on?","They're 40 riyals. Do you want to try them on?","It's 40 riyals. Do you want to try them in?","Their 40 riyals. Do you want to try on them?"],"answer":"They're 40 riyals. Do you want to try them on?","explanation":"Pronoun goes in the middle: try it on.","explanation_ar":"الضمير في الوسط."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS5-IMG01","prompt":"Sara and her mother at a traditional market stall choosing a scarf; the seller holding up colorful scarves with price tags. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Sara and her mother at a traditional market stall choosing a scarf; the seller holding up colorful scarves with price tags"},{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS5-IMG02","prompt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Clothes and Shopping”, speech bubbles left empty. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Clothes and Shopping”, speech bubbles left empty"},{"id":"GV-L02-U5-LS5-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Spin the Review Wheel”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Spin the Review Wheel"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U5-LS5-T1","script":"Sara: Excuse me, how much is this scarf? Seller: It's 40 riyals. Sara: It's lovely, but it's a little expensive. How much are those scarves? Seller: They're 25 riyals each. Sara: I like the green one. Can I see it, please? Seller: Of course. Here you are. Sara: Thanks! I'll take it. It's for my grandma – she'll love it!","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U5-LS5-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “At the Market: Language in Use”. Let’s learn object pronouns, prices with How much/How many, clothes words and contractions (unit review) together. Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Market day: half the class are sellers with price cards, half are shoppers with 100 pretend riyals. Shoppers ask \"How much is/are…? Can I try it on? Do you have it in…?\" and buy two things. Today you use all of Unit 5: object pronouns, How much is/are…?, How many…?, clothes words, a pair of, phrasal verbs and contractions. A shopping dialogue is polite: start with Excuse me, ask about the price and size, and say Thank you. Here are some examples. How much are these sneakers? They're 130 riyals. Can I try them on? Be careful! Some learners say: “How much this cap?.” That’s not right. We say: “How much is this cap?.” Don't forget is. Quick check: what is wrong with “Can I try on them?”? … Think! … It should be “Can I try them on?”. Great job! Now you can say: I can buy clothes in English.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]}],"unit_test":[{"q":"My cousins are here. I'm playing with ___.","options":["they","them","it","their"],"answer":"them","explanation":"they / plural things → them.","explanation_ar":"الجمع ← them."},{"q":"Please call ___. I'm lost!","options":["mine","I","me","my"],"answer":"me","explanation":"I → me after a verb or preposition.","explanation_ar":"I تصبح me بعد الفعل أو حرف الجر."},{"q":"Faisal is in the car. Wait for ___.","options":["them","his","he","him"],"answer":"him","explanation":"he → him.","explanation_ar":"he تصبح him."},{"q":"","options":["Lina has a kitten. She loves it.","Lina has a kitten. She loves them.","Lina has a kitten. She loves her it.","Lina has a kitten. She loves its."],"answer":"Lina has a kitten. She loves it.","explanation":"one thing → it.","explanation_ar":"الشيء الواحد ← it."},{"q":"","options":["Come to the park with our!","Come to the park with us!","Come to the park with ours us!","Come to the park with we!"],"answer":"Come to the park with us!","explanation":"we → us.","explanation_ar":"we تصبح us."},{"q":"How much ___ this belt?","options":["does","do","is","are"],"answer":"is","explanation":"One thing → How much is this/that…? – It's…","explanation_ar":"للمفرد: How much is this."},{"q":"How much are these boots? – ___","options":["They're 200 riyals.","They 200 riyals.","There are 200 riyals.","It's 200 riyals."],"answer":"They're 200 riyals.","explanation":"Plural → How much are these/those…? – They're…","explanation_ar":"للجمع: How much are these."},{"q":"How many ___ do you need?","options":["bages","a bag","bag","bags"],"answer":"bags","explanation":"Number → How many + plural noun?","explanation_ar":"للعدد: How many + جمع."},{"q":"","options":["How many is that cap?","How much is that cap?","How much are that cap?","How much that cap?"],"answer":"How much is that cap?","explanation":"One thing → How much is this/that…? – It's…","explanation_ar":"للمفرد: How much is this."},{"q":"___ brothers do you have? – Two.","options":["How","What much","How much","How many"],"answer":"How many","explanation":"Number → How many + plural noun?","explanation_ar":"للعدد: How many + جمع."},{"q":"I need ___ shoes for the wedding.","options":["an","a","one","a pair of"],"answer":"a pair of","explanation":"Two-part clothes → a pair of.","explanation_ar":"الملابس ذات الجزأين ← a pair of."},{"q":"This bag costs 3,000 riyals. It's ___.","options":["expensive","cheap","small","free"],"answer":"expensive","explanation":"cheap ↔ expensive; small ↔ large.","explanation_ar":"الأضداد."},{"q":"These gloves are too small. Do you have a bigger ___?","options":["cost","pair","size","price"],"answer":"size","explanation":"Choose the right clothes or shopping word.","explanation_ar":"اختر كلمة الملابس أو التسوّق المناسبة."},{"q":"","options":["I like this jacket. Can I try it in?","I like this jacket. Can I try on it?","I like this jacket. Can I try on?","I like this jacket. Can I try it on?"],"answer":"I like this jacket. Can I try it on?","explanation":"try on / put on / take off – pronoun in the middle (try it on).","explanation_ar":"الضمير في الوسط."},{"q":"It's warm inside. Take ___ your coat.","options":["up","in","on","off"],"answer":"off","explanation":"try on / put on / take off – pronoun in the middle (try it on).","explanation_ar":"الضمير في الوسط."},{"q":"Boys and men in Saudi Arabia wear a ___ to the mosque.","options":["glove","thobe","sock","dress"],"answer":"thobe","explanation":"Choose the right clothes or shopping word.","explanation_ar":"اختر كلمة الملابس أو التسوّق المناسبة."},{"q":"was not → ___","options":["wa'snt","wasnt","wasn't","was'nt"],"answer":"wasn't","explanation":"The apostrophe replaces the missing letter(s).","explanation_ar":"الفاصلة العلوية مكان الحرف المحذوف."},{"q":"","options":["My brother doesnt have a cap.","My brother doe'snt have a cap.","My brother doesn't have a cap.","My brother does'nt have a cap."],"answer":"My brother doesn't have a cap.","explanation":"Put the apostrophe exactly where the letter is missing.","explanation_ar":"ضع الفاصلة في مكانها الصحيح."},{"q":"","options":["It's very cheap!","Its very cheap!","It is' very cheap!","Its' very cheap!"],"answer":"It's very cheap!","explanation":"it's = it is; its = belongs to it.","explanation_ar":"it's تعني it is وits للملكية."},{"q":"","options":["The shop has it is own café.","The shop has its own café.","The shop has its' own café.","The shop has it's own café."],"answer":"The shop has its own café.","explanation":"it's = it is; its = belongs to it.","explanation_ar":"it's تعني it is وits للملكية."},{"q":"","options":["Their in the fitting room.","There in the fitting room.","They're in the fitting room.","Theyr'e in the fitting room."],"answer":"They're in the fitting room.","explanation":"they're = they are.","explanation_ar":"they're تعني they are."},{"q":"Choose the best line for a customer:","options":["Excuse me, how much are these socks?","Excuse me, how many are these socks?","Excuse me, how much is these socks?","Excuse me, how much these socks?"],"answer":"Excuse me, how much are these socks?","explanation":"Plural → How much are these/those…? – They're…","explanation_ar":"للجمع: How much are these."},{"q":"How can we fix it? \"its too big for i.\"","options":["It's too big for I.","It's too big for me.","Its too big for me.","it's too big for me."],"answer":"It's too big for me.","explanation":"I → me after a verb or preposition.","explanation_ar":"I تصبح me بعد الفعل أو حرف الجر."},{"q":"Do you like my new shoes? – Yes, I love ___!","options":["them","its","they","it"],"answer":"them","explanation":"they / plural things → them.","explanation_ar":"الجمع ← them."}],"theme_ar":"الملابس والتسوّق","essential_question_ar":"كيف نتخذ قرارات جيدة عندما نتسوّق؟","can_do":"I can talk about clothes, ask about prices and use object pronouns like me, him, her and them.","can_do_ar":"أستطيع أن أتحدث عن الملابس، وأسأل عن الأسعار، وأستخدم ضمائر المفعول مثل me وhim وher وthem."});
